    {
      "finding_id": "FND-000005",
      "document_id": "DOC-000001",
      "title": "Email Enumeration Possible During User Registration",
      "source_title_block": {
        "block_number": 331,
        "paragraph_number": 308,
        "style": "EvvoH2"
      },
      "extraction": {
        "start_block_number": 331,
        "end_block_number": 354,
        "block_count": 24,
        "non_empty_block_count": 18
      },
      "raw_blocks": [
        {
          "block_number": 331,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 308,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "EvvoH2",
          "text": "Email Enumeration Possible During User Registration",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 332,
          "block_type": "table",
          "paragraph_number": null,
          "table_number": 24,
          "style": null,
          "text": null,
          "rows": [
            {
              "row_number": 1,
              "cells": [
                "SEVERITY",
                "LOW"
              ]
            },
            {
              "row_number": 2,
              "cells": [
                "AFFECTED TARGETS",
                "https://eform.brightree.com.sg/users/sign_up"
              ]
            },
            {
              "row_number": 3,
              "cells": [
                "CWE-ID",
                "CWE-204: Observable Response Discrepancy"
              ]
            },
            {
              "row_number": 4,
              "cells": [
                "IMPACT (Potential)",
                "The application discloses whether a username already exists during the user registration process through distinguishable server responses. An attacker may leverage this behavior to enumerate valid usernames, facilitating subsequent attacks such as password spraying, credential stuffing, or targeted brute-force attacks."
              ]
            },
            {
              "row_number": 5,
              "cells": [
                "RETEST STATUS",
                ""
              ]
            },
            {
              "row_number": 6,
              "cells": [
                "Affected User Roles",
                "No authentication required"
              ]
            },
            {
              "row_number": 7,
              "cells": [
                "CVSS SCORE",
                "5.3 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_number": 333,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 309,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 334,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 310,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Observation",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 335,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 311,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "The user registration functionality was assessed to determine whether the application discloses information about existing user accounts.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 336,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 312,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "During testing, it was observed that the application returns different responses depending on whether the submitted username already exists in the system. When an existing username is provided, the server returns a specific error message indicating that the username has already been registered. Conversely, when a non-existing username is supplied, the application proceeds with the registration process or returns a different response.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 337,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 313,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "The distinguishable responses allow an unauthenticated attacker to determine whether a username exists within the application, resulting in a username enumeration vulnerability.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 338,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 314,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 339,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 315,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Exploitation",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 340,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 316,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Navigate to the application's user registration page.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 341,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 317,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Submit a registration request using an existing email and observe that the application returns a response indicating that the email already exists.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 342,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 318,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 343,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 319,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Repeat the request using a email that does not exist in the system. Observe that the application redirects the request to the login page without indicating that the username already exists.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 344,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 320,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "By comparing the server responses, an attacker can systematically enumerate valid email registered within the application.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 345,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 321,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Recommendation",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 346,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 322,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "List Paragraph",
          "text": "Return a generic response for all registration attempts regardless of whether the submitted username already exists.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 347,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 323,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "List Paragraph",
          "text": "Avoid exposing detailed validation messages that reveal the existence of user accounts.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 348,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 324,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "List Paragraph",
          "text": "Perform duplicate account validation internally without disclosing the result to the client.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 349,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 325,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "List Paragraph",
          "text": "Implement rate limiting and CAPTCHA on the registration endpoint to reduce automated enumeration attempts.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 350,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 326,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "List Paragraph",
          "text": "Monitor and alert on excessive registration requests that may indicate username enumeration activity.",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 351,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 327,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 352,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 328,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "Re-Test Verification Result:",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
          "block_number": 353,
          "block_type": "paragraph",
          "paragraph_number": 329,
          "table_number": null,
          "style": "Normal",
          "text": "",
          "rows": null
        },
        {
